\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Composition of the three fine-tuning sets, each of 6,400 samples (targets equal realised values for all three sets). Scenario groups: A obstacle avoidance and construction, B junctions, C hazards and emergencies, D highway and merging, E vulnerable road users and dynamic conflicts, F baseline and signal compliance. The name hazard-heavy refers to the higher shares of groups A and C, not to the observed hazard share in the row "Brake / hazard share".}}{7}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
